    "message": "feat(providers): Claude subscription OAuth provider, gated to the Claude Code CLI\n\nAdds `anthropic_oauth`: routes requests with the OAuth credential from a Claude\nPro/Max subscription, discovered from Claude Code's own\n~/.claude/.credentials.json or obtained by `mcc-anthropic-oauth-login` (PKCE).\n\nANTHROPIC DOES NOT PERMIT THIS. Their Claude Code legal-and-compliance page\nstates plan OAuth credentials are for Claude Code and Claude.ai only, that\nthird-party developers may not offer Claude.ai login or route requests through\nFree/Pro/Max credentials, and that they may enforce without prior notice. This\nships at the operator's explicit instruction, for their own account, after that\npolicy was quoted to them. docs/ANTHROPIC-SUBSCRIPTION.md is the disclaimer and\nsays so plainly rather than claiming an \"inside Claude Code\" exemption that does\nnot exist.\n\nThe gate is the part worth reviewing. Claude Code stamps an attribution line at\nthe head of the system prompt, in the request body:\n\n    x-anthropic-billing-header: cc_version=2.1.235.2db; cc_entrypoint=cli;\n\nMeasured on real traffic: the terminal CLI reports cc_entrypoint=cli and the\nPython Agent SDK reports cc_entrypoint=sdk-py. Because it travels in the body, a\nproxy can neither forge it for traffic it did not receive nor strip it from\ntraffic it did. So the provider refuses, by default, any request that does not\nreport `cli`, and points it at the `anthropic` (Console API key) provider\ninstead. That turns \"only within Claude Code\" from a promise in a README into\nsomething the router enforces, and specifically stops Agent SDK traffic -- the\ncase the policy names -- from silently borrowing the subscription.\n\nAlso here: the full Claude Code header set (both anthropic-beta values, x-app,\nthe claude-cli User-Agent), the `cc_` tool-name prefix the OAuth surface\nrequires, normalised back out of response frames so nothing downstream sees it,\nand a new `credential_discoverable` descriptor flag so a provider that finds its\nown credential does not fail the \"key is not set\" check while still offering an\nAdmin field.\n\nCredential handling: MCC's own store is ~/.fcc/anthropic_oauth.json at mode 0600.\nClaude Code's file is read-only to MCC and never refreshed in place -- rotating\nit would log out the user's real client. Claude Code stores expiry in\nmilliseconds and the token endpoint returns seconds; both normalise, with a test.\n\nVerification.\n- 24 new tests; full suite 4211 passed, 26 skipped.\n- 6 failures, all tests/scripts/test_installers.py PowerShell -- the documented\n  irreducible baseline, identical to unmodified fork/main.\n- Guards mutation-tested and confirmed to fail by name: widening the entrypoint\n  match fails 7 tests including the two refusal cases; dropping the ms->s\n  expiry normalisation fails the credential test.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty, suppression grep all clean.\n\nTwo of my own mistakes caught by the contract tests and fixed rather than\nworked around: cli/ may not import a provider submodule (registered a documented\nIMPORT_EXCEPTIONS edge, matching the chatgpt_oauth precedent), and my first\nsmoke-config check called detect_available_sources(), which reads the real\nfilesystem and made the suite depend on whether the machine running it is logged\nin to Claude Code.\n\nNot done: no live request has been made against api.anthropic.com with a\nsubscription credential. The gate, headers, tool prefixing, credential loading\nand refresh are tested against fakes; a real round trip is not, and whether\nAnthropic accepts or refuses this traffic is unknown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
